\date{2024-08-12}
\taxon{Lemma}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\import{common}

\p{
Given a [[hott-000I]] #{L} and a precategory \category{C} whose isomorphism-types are #{L}-local, then if \category{C} is #{L}-extensional its type of objects is #{\suspension L}-local.
}

\proof{
  The codomain of the map #{(x =_{\category{C}} y) \to (x \cong_{\category{C}} y)} is #{L}-local by assumption, hence by one of the [closure properties of orthogonal maps](hott-0005) the domain is #{L}-local if and only if the map is. TODO: THIS IS WRONG!!
}
